# Topic: a frame that never ends gives the pages its collector freed back
#
# What it does: while cold touches are tracked (patch 13), a page of collected objects waits for the next frame
# (lua_coldframe), since the list of marked objects may point into it. Once the pages kept in a frame pass 8 MiB (or 64
# bytes an entry of the list, if more), and when a full list of a million entries or more would grow, the list drops its
# entries into the kept pages, its entries for free blocks and for objects no mark is on, and its repeats, and the pages
# go back to the allocator. Each marked object keeps one entry, so the marks the next frame clears, every count and the
# heap's totals stay as they were.
#
# Why upstream lacks it: upstream has no cold touches (patch 13), and frees a page as soon as its objects are collected.
# Kept to the frame's end, a script loop that never yields kept every page its collector freed: a string grown one letter
# at a time took the process past 2 GB in about a second while gcinfo read 2 MB, where a playing client and a server keep
# their memory flat.

diff --git a/luau/VM/src/lgc.cpp b/luau/VM/src/lgc.cpp
index 3605a55c..c3f36654 100644
--- a/luau/VM/src/lgc.cpp
+++ b/luau/VM/src/lgc.cpp
